WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.768
-Ralph, over the years,
there have been a lot of rumors

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:04.236
floating around
about the "Karate Kid" movies.

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:06.206
I have a few here
I'd like your thoughts on.

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.340
Sound good?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.741
-I'm good.
-Alright. Let's do it.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:12.111
It's time for "The Final Word:
Cobra Kai Edition."

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:16.415
-♪ It's "The Final Word:
Cobra Kai Edition" ♪

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:18.584
Alright, first rumor,

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:21.120
"The Karate Kid"
is such an iconic title,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.957 line:0%
but is it true that
you didn't like it at first?

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.825 line:0%
-That is true. That is true.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.560 line:0%
We thought -- I thought,
and I was not the only one,

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.798 line:0%
thought it was kind of a hokey,
kind of cheesy title

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.633 line:0%
for a movie being directed
by the guy who made "Rocky"

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:37.269 line:0%
and all this stuff.
But maybe it was foreshadowing.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:38.972 line:0%
I maybe thought
if I ever got the part,

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.007 line:0%
I'd have to carry the damn thing
for the rest of my life.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.208 line:0%
Maybe that was it.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.411 line:0%
-And be The Karate Kid, yeah.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:47.013
Follow-up, what did you think
the movie should've been called?

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:50.349
-If I came up with that great
title, we might've had a shot.

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:52.251
You know, it was called --
-Any bad ones?

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:54.887
-Yeah, I think John Avildsen,
our director, said,

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:57.790
"Maybe it's
'East meets West in West'?"

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.026
I was like --
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:02.295
Yeah, we'll have people
do a little math

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.363
when they're going
to see the movie.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.697
-Exactly. Like,
what does that mean?

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.433
And I think it was called
"The Moment of Truth"

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:10.537
in many countries when "karate"
had a negative connotation

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.539
in certain territories.
-Oh, really?

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.473
-So it was called
"The Moment of Truth."

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:16.176
-"The Moment of Truth."
I don't mind that one.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:17.543
-"Moment of Truth II,"
"Moment of Truth --"

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:19.679
It's just not working.
-Yeah, that's true, yeah, yeah.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.014
Alright, here we go, second one.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.183
Everyone knows you
as Daniel LaRusso.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:26.085 line:0%
But is it true other people were
considered for the role, too?

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:28.588 line:0%
-No. Yes.
-I'm assuming, right?

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.590 line:0%
-It was all me.
It was all me all the time.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:34.793 line:0%
No, I was found early.
I was cast very early.

00:01:34.793 --> 00:01:36.395 line:0%
But it was like
one of those test deals

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:38.331 line:0%
where you're not in yet.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.300 line:0%
And I remember walking by
and seeing Charlie Sheen

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.770 line:0%
hanging outside
Jerry Weintraub's bungalow.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.237 line:0%
Like, what's Charlie doing here?

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:47.340 line:0%
And I heard --

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.474 line:0%
-"Hey, bud,
nice to see you again."

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:49.909 line:0%
-"Yeah, good to see you.
What are you doing here?

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.911 line:0%
You don't look like
an Italian guy from Jersey."

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.512 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
-"Uh, hey."

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:56.649 line:0%
And Downey Jr. --
-I heard Nick Cage.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.118 line:0%
-Nick Cage, I think.
I remember --

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.820 line:0%
Yeah, and Robert Downey Jr.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.988 line:0%
Robert Downey Jr.
also did the workshop

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:04.957 line:0%
of the part I did
in "The Outsiders."

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:07.660 line:0%
So I was doing pretty good
with Downey Jr. at that point,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.363 line:0%
and then it just --
Like Iron Man, it took off.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.932 line:0%
-Yeah, what happened to that?
-Nah, it's great.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:16.335 line:0%
-Oh, this is an interesting one
they got off the Internet.

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:18.170 line:0%
And I don't know why.
You have to explain this to me.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.239 line:0%
Do you write Thor comics?

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:24.210 line:0%
-Ah, no.
That's another Ralph Macchio.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.411 line:0%
It's amazing.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.114 line:0%
I learned about this
when someone was like,

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:30.283 line:0%
"Dude, love your movies.
Thanks for Thor!"

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.751 line:0%
And I was like, "Okay."

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.921 line:0%
And, "Why were you thanked for
Thor at the end of the movie?"

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.822 line:0%
And I said,
"Let me do some research."

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.659 line:0%
So, there is
a very famous Ralph Macchio

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.263 line:0%
who's a part of Stanley's team
at Marvel and writes comics.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.798 line:0%
I've never met him. I wonder
if he knows who the hell I am.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.566 line:0%
-Wow. Amazing. That's wild.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:49.335 line:0%
-Isn't that wild?
-I never heard that. Yeah.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.470
At the end of "The Karate Kid,"

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.939
you famously win
the All Valley Championship

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:54.974
with the crane kick.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.876
Now, before
we get into it, okay,

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.944
I want to show everyone
the scene we're talking about.

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:02.181
Here's the famous crane kick
from "The Karate Kid."

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:04.550
-No mercy! No mercy!

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.219
[ Shouts indistinctly ]

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.120
Finish him!

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.858 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:14.360
-Fight!

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.163
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:21.200
-Come on. Come on!

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.170
That was the famous scene from
"East Meets West Goes West."

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.573
And -- No, I hate
to bring this up,

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:27.806
but people have asked
this question.

00:03:27.806 --> 00:03:29.074
-Do you? Do you really?
Go ahead.

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:30.909
-Yeah, exactly. I think --

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:32.144
Well, no, I have --
-Go ahead.

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:33.246
-This first one, I don't know.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:36.849 line:0%
Was the kick actually legal?

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:42.087 line:0%
-Yes, it's become
an Internet, um, fan theory,

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:43.489 line:0%
is that the kick was not legal.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:45.925 line:0%
Here's my theory.
No, here's the truth.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.726 line:0%
-Whoa! That's what
I'm talking about. Yes.

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:49.495 line:0%
-Here's the truth,
'cause it's been a while,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.965 line:0%
and I've been fighting off
these theories a long time.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:55.901 line:0%
Listen, Mr. Miyagi
was the ultimate teacher,

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.705 line:0%
so, and LaRusso had him
as his trainer.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:01.341 line:0%
And as the superior trainer --
He's basically the human Yoda --

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.342 line:0%
You don't bet against Yoda.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:05.411 line:0%
You don't bet against Miyagi.
That's number one.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:08.781 line:0%
Number two, I would say, is that
LaRusso, how did he train?

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.517 line:0%
He trained over a couple of
weeks time by household chores,

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.553 line:0%
never having the ability
or privilege

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.454 line:0%
to have a sparring partner.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:18.024 line:0%
His opponent there, bud,
was like, you know,

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:21.227 line:0%
in combat-ready training
for years for this event.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:23.996 line:0%
LaRusso was injured
in the final fight, correct?

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:27.533 line:0%
-That's true.
-He was injured by an illegal --

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.867 line:0%
-You really have
thought about this.

00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:30.903 line:0%
-Don't get me started.
-Oh, no, I want to! I want to!

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.671 line:0%
-They mentioned
we were going to go here.

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:37.309 line:0%
An illegal leg sweep
by a teammate of said opponent.

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:41.013 line:0%
And so, not to mention --

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.782 line:0%
-"Said opponent."

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.017 line:0%
It's like we're in court.
-I'm in a courtroom.

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:47.519 line:0%
-Your Honor! Your Honor.
-It's "My Cousin Vinny" now.

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:49.355 line:0%
I've just moved
to another movie.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.492 line:0%
So, and if you look
at the tape, Jimmy,

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.693 line:0%
if you look at the tape,
not only,

00:04:54.693 --> 00:04:57.163 line:0%
not only does the ref say
"Point, winner" --

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.598 line:0%
A win is a win --

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:02.134 line:0%
The opponent, who shall remain
nameless at this point,

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:05.605 line:0%
literally arguably charged,
ran into the kick.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:08.307 line:0%
LaRusso had nothing to do
but defend himself.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:09.975 line:0%
-There you go.
The kick was legal.

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:11.977 line:0%
What do you -- True. I agree.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:13.846 line:0%
How can you fight --

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.681 line:0%
Case closed on that one.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:16.548 line:0%
-I rest my case.

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:19.051 line:0%
-This one is just --

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.686 line:0%
I think I have my own theory
on this one.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:22.755 line:0%
It's not a real theory for me.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.258 line:0%
Was Daniel LaRusso
really the underdog,

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:28.027 line:0%
or is he actually
kind of a bully?

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:31.063 line:0%
-Mm, yeah, that's not even --
Listen, I believe

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:34.300 line:0%
that no one was not rooting
for Daniel LaRusso in 1984.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:37.103 line:0%
I -- Let me do it this way.

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:38.404 line:0%
I'm using you as an example,

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.306 line:0%
someone of great character
and judgment.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.507 line:0%
-Thank you.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.877 line:0%
-Okay, I've seen
more than a handful of sketches

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:47.313 line:0%
that pay homage
to "The Karate Kid" film.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.581 line:0%
-Yes.

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:51.217 line:0%
-You are always wearing
the Miyagi-Do headband.

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.384 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:54.954 line:0%
-You would never
endorse a bully.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.223 line:0%
So therein lies
the answer to the question.

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.491 line:0%
-Wow. So there --

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:00.359 line:0%
See, I would never
endorse a bully, you're right.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.328 line:0%
-No, you're not putting on
a black headband.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:04.229 line:0%
You're putting on
Miyagi's headband,

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:06.933 line:0%
which is LaRusso's headband,
which is the hero of the --

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.300 line:0%
-Who was an underdog. Thank you.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.902 line:0%
Daniel LaRusso.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.337
[ Cheers and applause,
both laugh ]

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:13.439
We love you. There you have it.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.141
Ralph, thank you so much
for being --

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:18.711
The new season of "Cobra Kai"
is streaming now on Netflix!

